From: MacSW maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Register NSAppSleepDisabled so App Nap stays off.

transformProcessToForeground begins an activity with
NSActivityUserInitiatedAllowingIdleSystemSleep to keep App Nap away from
every windowed Wine process (unless HKCU\Software\Wine\Mac Driver\EnableAppNap
is "y"). On macOS 27 that activity no longer does it completely: about 40 s
after a Wine app stops being the frontmost app, macOS clamps the whole task
to utility QoS (task base priority 31 -> 20, every thread's maximum priority
20). SOLIDWORKS then runs a rebuild, an open or the rest of its start-up at
utility QoS, below every default-QoS thread of the other apps. Measured with
proc_pid_rusage (per-QoS CPU time) and PROC_PIDTASKINFO (pti_priority):
 * a native AppKit app with the same activity: clamped to 20 after 40-50 s;
   with NSActivityLatencyCritical added, or with NSAppSleepDisabled in its
   defaults (persistent domain, or registered before NSApplication exists):
   stays at 31; the Info.plist keys NSAppSleepDisabled / LSAppNapIsDisabled
   do not help; registering the default after NSApplication exists does not
   help either.
 * SOLIDWORKS in a clone bottle (shell launch and SOLIDWORKS.app): all 64
   threads at 20, more than half of the start-up CPU time at utility QoS.

run_cocoa_app() now registers NSAppSleepDisabled = YES in the registration
domain right before it creates the NSApplication, when App Nap is disabled
(enable_app_nap false, the default). It acts for every launch path (MacSW,
SOLIDWORKS.app, a shell) because it does not depend on a bundle identifier;
the user's own defaults still win over the registration domain.
Wine 11.16 has the same code without this default.
Details: docs/cpu-scheduling-night.md.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_main.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_main.m
index 8c9507a..7fd71fa 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_main.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_main.m
@@ -70,6 +70,13 @@ static void run_cocoa_app(void* info)
     {
         if (!NSApp)
         {
+            /* MacSW: the NSActivityUserInitiated activity that transformProcessToForeground begins no
+               longer keeps App Nap away completely: macOS 27 clamps a non-frontmost app that holds
+               only that activity to utility QoS (priority 20) after about 40 s.  NSAppSleepDisabled
+               turns App Nap off; it must be registered before the NSApplication exists. */
+            if (!enable_app_nap)
+                [[NSUserDefaults standardUserDefaults] registerDefaults:
+                    [NSDictionary dictionaryWithObject:[NSNumber numberWithBool:YES] forKey:@"NSAppSleepDisabled"]];
             [WineApplication sharedApplication];
             created_app = TRUE;
         }
